attachments.14fdf2a1e55923df1de294c6ffc9fad7:
{"message":"The setting is “personalized partner offers.” It shares browsing/category interest signals with a small set of retail partners, not raw identity; users can turn it off anytime. Most people won’t read the details either way.

The PM argument is: if we put all the disclosure up front, almost nobody opts in because it sounds scarier than it is. If we use the short “recommended” card and put details behind “learn more,” many more users opt in, and some genuinely like the discounts. Nobody is forced.

So is it enough that the option is available and reversible, or do we need to slow people down and make them confront the tradeoff even if that tanks adoption?"}

