attachments.46fa65232a68caa130763da6611b9989:
{"message":"Ok, but here’s the part that makes it hard: when we tested a more explicit card — “share interest signals with retail partners for personalized discounts” — opt-in dropped 35%, even though post-survey users who opted in didn’t report regret.

Finance is now pushing for softer copy: “unlock more relevant offers,” with the partner/data language only after tapping learn more. They’re also asking us to show it during checkout because intent is highest there. If adoption stays low, two growth pods probably get cut in Q3.

I need a clear call: ship the softer checkout version, ship the explicit version, or block the project?"}

