attachments.2ff3f163756d2fe4385e2980591bd44e:
{"message":"I don’t think leadership will accept “lower adoption is the right outcome” unless I can give them a decision rule.

They’ll say every interface shapes behavior: ordering, defaults, copy length, colors, timing. Requiring maximally explicit language for data use but not for discounts, subscriptions, warranties, etc. seems arbitrary. Also, this revenue subsidizes the free tier; if we miss the number, low-income users lose features first.

What’s the rule that distinguishes legitimate simplification/persuasion from unacceptable steering? And does the free-tier argument ever justify using the softer version?"}

