{"message":"One last edge case. Suppose we don’t change the factual disclosure, but we personalize presentation.

For users who usually accept convenience features, show the “recommended / unlock relevant offers” framing first with disclosure visible below. For privacy-sensitive users, show the explicit data-sharing framing first because they’re more likely to care. For users who abandon settings screens, show it during checkout; for others, show it in account settings.

Product says this respects preferences because we’re matching communication style to the user. Critics would call it susceptibility targeting. Is that materially different from the softer-copy issue?"}
